      "message": "\u003e I thought that hypervisor may not return actual phys without your crosvm change. Am I misunderstanding?\n\nCorrect but we also can\u0027t assign devices without the other crosvm changes that also have yet to be merged into AOSP, anyway. So I\u0027m considering _all_ those changes (i.e. the 3 commits at ag/25368747, which have ~15 upstream commits  squashed) as one atomic diff: if we\u0027re already merging code assuming that crosvm supports DA (ag/25370734), then we can also merge code that assumes ag/25368747, as long as we guarantee that AOSP never triggers it (as you said).\n\n\u003e let\u0027s just stop booting when validation fails. It shouldn\u0027t break anything\n\nThis is based on the assumption that pvmfw (more specifically, `DeviceAssignmentInfo::parse`) would never issue the verification HVCs unless it find assigned devices in the crosvm DT, right? That makes sense but see other thread.",
